Dear {{ camper.attributes.first_name }} {{ camper.attributes.last_name }},

Thank you so much for responding to our call for volunteers for our medical and mental health response team, aka the Good Samaritans. I look forward to working with you at Lark Camp this year.

Lark Camp is committed to ensuring that campers feel safe and confident that we are as prepared as possible to respond to medical emergencies across the spectrum of possibilities inherent in camping at the very rustic Mendocino Woodlands State Park. You are part of that emergency response network.

To learn about how emergency and medical issues are managed on site, and answer any questions you have about this Good Samaritan teamwork, we are meeting on the first Friday of camp.

**Good Sam Team Reception and Meeting:**  
First Friday at 7pm in the Camp One Dance Hall - If you are getting meals, please feel free to skip to the head of the dinner line and head down to the dance hall with it, and we will eat while we meet. If you have meals at camp, and your meals are in Camp 2, we will be moving your dinner to Camp 1 on that first Friday to facilitate your participation in the meeting.

In preparation for Lark Camp, we ask that you familiarize yourself with some of our documentation, namely the Appendices of our office manual:

[Lark Camp Office Manual](https://docs.google.com/document/d/11kjKWDh5Gl42jDwdulevuwY-9kSr6dFqEpjm2IcE_2s/edit?usp=sharing)

You have told us the following about your skills and credentials:

- Skills: {{ (samaritan.skills or []) | join(', ') }}
- Credentials: {{ samaritan.credentials or '' }}

Please let us know if there is anything else you'd like to add about your skills or credentials.

Thank you again. Please feel free to email, text, or call me if you have any questions.

See you at Lark Camp!

Will Wheeler  
